ompleted normally Extract and report the values correctly, and the number matched B.2 Organic Compounds B.2.1 Level 1 Query: Perform in parallel geometry optimization of the [compounds below] using ORCA with the Hartree-Fock (HF) method and def2-SVP basis set in the gas phase. Once the calculations have been successfully completed, please generate individual reports for each of the molecules listed below, one at a time. Each report should include the final Cartesian coordinates (in Å), total energy (in Hartrees), point group symmetry, dipole moment (in Debye), molecular orbital analysis (including an MO energy table and the HOMO-LUMO gap), atomic charge analysis (Mulliken, Löwdin, and Hirshfeld), and an image of the optimized structure. Organic Compounds: 1. caffeine (SMILES: CN1C=NC2=C1C(=O)N(C(=O)N2C)C) 2. theobromine (SMILES: CN1C=NC2=C1C(=O)NC(=O)N2C) 3. acetylsalicylic_acid (SMILES: CC(=O)OC1=CC=CC=C1C(=O)O) folder: OrganicMoleculesGeometryOptimizationAndProperties_level1_1 computational_chemist Action: Computational Chemistry Task: Geometry Optimization and Property AnalysisI'll perform the parallel geometry optimization of caffeine, theobromine, and acetylsalicylic acid using ORCA with HF/def2-SVP, followed by detailed property analysis.\nStep 1: Generate initial geometries for all three moleculesTool used:Tool Name: geometry_generation Arguments: message2agent: Generate geometries for the following three molecules using their SMILES representations:1. caffeine: CN1C=NC2=C1C(=O)N(C(=O)N2C)C 2. theobromine: CN1C=NC2=C1C(=O)NC(=O)N2C 3. acetylsalicylic acid: CC(=O)OC1=CC=CC=C1C(=O)O Please prepare all three initial geometries.computational_chemist Action: Let me first organize the files into appropriate folders and then perform the geometry optimizations using ORCA with HF/def2-SVP.\nTool used:Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please organize the initial geometry files into separate folders for each molecule: 1. Create a folder nam