r each molecule 3. Geometry Optimization:• Performed preliminary optimization using xtb • Conducted full HF/def2-SVP optimizations with frequency calculations • Verified all structures reached stable minima (no imaginary frequencies) 4. Data Extraction and Visualization: • Extracted comprehensive data from output files including: -Final Cartesian coordinates -Total energy values -Dipole moments -Molecular orbital energies and HOMO-LUMO gaps -Atomic charge analyses (Mulliken, Löwdin, and Hirshfeld) • Created visualizations of the optimized structures 5. Report Generation: • Generated detailed reports for each molecule in Markdown format • Saved reports in a dedicated 'reports' directory Results Summary: Molecule Total Energy (Hartrees) HOMO-LUMO Gap (eV) Dipole Moment (Debye) Caffeine -675.83732469 11.81 4.33 Theobromine -636.83781921 11.83 4.94 Acetylsalicylic Acid -644.47944566 11.70 2.30The reports containing all requested information (coordinates, energies, symmetry, dipole moments, MO analysis, charge analysis, and structure images) can be found in the 'reports' directory: -reports/-caffeine_report.md -reports/theobromine_report.md -reports/acetylsalicylic_acid_report.md All calculations were performed successfully and the requested analysis has been completed.18. 3-methylbutanoate_anion: charge = -1, multiplicity = 1 19. diisopropylamide_anion: charge = -1, multiplicity = 1 20. diisopropylammonium_cation: charge = +1, multiplicity = 1 For all calculations, use ORCA with the HF/def2-SVP level of theory. computational_chemist Action: Step 3: Generate reports for each molecule I'll now generate comprehensive reports for each molecule by extracting the requested data from the ORCA output files. I'll start with the first molecule and continue with the rest. 3.1 Caffeine Report Tool used: Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please extract the following information from the caffeine/caffeine_HF_OPT_-FREQ/caffeine_HF_OPT_FREQ.out file: 1. Fi