_OPT_FREQ.inp 2. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_pris-matic_OPT_FREQ.inp 3. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antipris-matic_0_OPT_FREQ.inp 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_an-tiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_-FREQ.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_-OPT_FREQ.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: The SCF blocks from the requested input files are as follows: 1. tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.inp \\%scf AutotraH false MaxIter 500 end 2. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ.inp \\%scf AutotraH false MaxIter 500 end 3. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_-FREQ.inp \\%scf AutotraH false MaxIter 500 end 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_-FREQ.inp \\%scf AutotraH false MaxIter 500• All jobs failed with an error: \"Unknown identifier in SCF block line 13: Last token: TIGHTSCF\" • Fixed the input files by replacing \"TightSCF true\" with \"ConvCriteria Tight\" 3. Second submission attempt:• Jobs failed again with error: \"Unknown identifier in SCF block line 13: Last token: CON-VCRITERIA\" • Modified the input files by removing the problematic convergence criteria settings entirely 4. Final successful submission:• All five jobs completed successfully with \"ORCA TERMINATED NORMALLY\" status • Each job directory now contains the expected output files (.out, .xyz, _trj.xyz) The following ORCA geometry optimization and frequency calculations for the Ce(III) complexes are now complete: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ 2. tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ 3. tricapped_-trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ 5. capped_-square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ All output files are available in their respective job directories. Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please check the output files for all five calculations to determine if they converged successfully. For each calculation, check the corresponding .out file in the respective folder and look for \"ORCA TERMINATED NORMALLY\" message and verify that both the geometry optimization and frequency calculations completed successfully. Please report if there are any errors or warnings that need attention.interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used:Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information'] interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_-OPT_FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information'] Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information'] Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information'] Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_-FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information'] interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information', 'SCF HESSIAN'] Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_-OPT_FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information', 'SCF HESSIAN'] Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information', 'SCF HESSIAN'] Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information', 'SCF HESSIAN'] Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_-FREQ.out query_keys: ['convergence_information', 'SCF HESSIAN'] interact_with_os_and_files Action:All five calculations were checked for convergence and completion of both geometry optimization and frequency (Hessian) calculations. Here are the results: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ:• SCF converged after 6 cycles.• Geometry optimization converged successfully.• Frequency (Hessian) calculation completed successfully.• Note: \"Only C1 symmetry has been detected, increase convergence thresholds\" (not a critical error, just a note). 2. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ:• SCF converged after 6 cycles.• Geometry optimization converged successfully.• Frequency (Hessian) calculation completed successfully.• Note: \"Only C1 symmetry has been detected, increase convergence thresholds\". 3. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ:• SCF converged after 6 cycles.• Geometry optimization converged successfully.• Frequency (Hessian) calculation completed successfully.• Note: \"Only C1 symmetry has been detected, increase convergence thresholds\". 4. tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ:• SCF converged after 6 cycles.• Geometry optimization converged successfully.• Frequency (Hessian) calculation completed successfully.• Note: \"Only C1 symmetry has been detected, increase convergence thresholds\". 5. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ:• SCF converged after 6 cycles.• Geometry optimization converged successfully.• Frequency (Hessian) calculation completed successfully.• Note: \"Only C1 symmetry has been detected, increase convergence thresholds\". No errors or critical warnings were found. All calculations terminated normally and completed both geometry optimization and frequency calculations successfully. The only repeated note is about C1 symmetry and convergence thresholds, which is informational and not an error.perform_dft_calculation Action: Tool used:Tool Name: update_global_memory Arguments: log_content: Completed geometry optimization with frequency calculations (OPT FREQ) for five Ce complex conformers using ORCA with the PBE0 functional, def2-SVP basis set, def2-ECP for Ce, D4 dispersion, and RIJCOSX approximation. All calculations converged successfully.perform_dft_calculation Action: I have successfully completed the geometry optimization with frequency calculations for all five Ce complex conformers using ORCA. Here's a summary of what was done: 1. Created job folders for each conformer with appropriate naming: • cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ • tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ • tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ • capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ • capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ 2. Generated ORCA input files with the specified settings: • Functional: PBE0 • Basis set: def2-SVP with def2-ECP for Ce • Dispersion: D4 • RIJCOSX approximation • DEFGRID2 integration grid • SCF autotraH: OFF • 16 cores per calculation • Max iterations: 500 for both SCF and geometry optimization • Charge: 0, Multiplicity: 2 3. Run all calculations in parallel using ORCA 4. Verified the results:• All five calculations completed successfully with \"ORCA TERMINATED NORMALLY\" • Geometry optimizations converged successfully for all conformers • Frequency calculations completed successfully for all conformers • No critical errors were found in any calculation The output files for each calculation are available in their respective job folders, including the optimized geometries (.xyz files) and full output files (.out) containing the calculated properties. Tool Name: remove_imaginary_frequency Arguments: message2agent: Please check for and remove imaginary frequencies from all five Ce complex conformers' DFT optimizations: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ 2. tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ 3. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ 5. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ remove_imaginary_frequency Action: I'll check for and remove imaginary frequencies from all five Ce complex conformers. First, let's check if any of the optimized structures have imaginary frequencies.\nTool used:Tool Name: check_imaginary_frequency Arguments:output_file_path_list: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.out', 'tri_-tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.out', 'tricapped_trigonal_pris-matic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ.out', 'capped_square_antipris-matic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ.out', 'capped_square_an-tiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ.out'] remove_imaginary_frequency Action:Based on the check, I've found imaginary frequencies in two of the conformers: 1. cn9_YICLED_-OPT_FREQ: Imaginary frequency of -131.99 cm -¹ in mode 6 2. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ: Imaginary frequency of -81.23 cm -¹ in mode 6The other three conformers (tri_tri_mer_capped, tricapped_trigonal_prismatic, and capped_square_-antiprismatic_0) don't have imaginary frequencies. Let's now generate trajectory files for the two structures with imaginary frequencies:Tool used: Tool Name: generate_trajectory_files Arguments: output_file_path_list: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.out', 'capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_-FREQ.out'] number_of_mode_list: [6, 6] remove_imaginary_frequency Action: Now, I'll parse the trajectory files to generate distorted xyz coordinates along the imaginary modes: Tool used: Tool Name: parse_distored_xyz_image Arguments: xyz_trajectory_file_names: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_-FREQ.out.v006.xyz', 'capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antipris-matic_1_OPT_FREQ.out.v006.xyz'] distored_xyz_file_names: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz', 'capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz'] remove_imaginary_frequency Action: Now I'll submit the distorted structures for new geometry optimization and frequency calculations to eliminate the imaginary frequencies: Tool used:Tool Name: perform_dft_calculation Arguments: message2agent: Please make sure to read the cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_-FREQ.inp and capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ.inp files and use the exact same configuration for the new calculations, simply replace the xyz file in the geometry line. The new calculations are about performing opt and freq calculation with the cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz and capped_square_-antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz files. Please name the output files with a \"_removed\" suffix. I'll perform the new calculations using the distorted geometries while maintaining the exact same ORCA configuration from the original input files. Let me first read the existing input files to understand their configuration:Tool used: Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please read the following input files and show their contents: 1. cn9_YICLED_-OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp 2. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/-capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: The contents of the requested input files are as follows: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp ! OPT FREQ PBE0 def2-SVP D4 RIJCOSX DEFGRID2 TightSCF \\%maxcore 4000 \\%pal nprocs 16 end \\%basis Basis \"def2-SVP\" ECP \"def2-ECP\" end \\%scf AutotraH false MaxIter 500 end \\%geom MaxIter 500 coordsys redundant cartfallback true ReducePrint true end \\%output Print[ P\\_Basis ] 2 Print[ P\\_MOs ] 1 Print[P\\_hirshfeld] 1 end * xyzfile 0 2 cn9\\_YICLED\\_0\\_nunpairedes\\_0\\_charge\\_0\\_xtb.xyz 2. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_-FREQ.inp ! OPT FREQ PBE0 def2-SVP D4 RIJCOSX DEFGRID2 TightSCF \\%maxcore 4000 \\%pal nprocs 16 end \\%basis Basis \"def2-SVP\" ECP \"def2-ECP\" end \\%scf AutotraH false MaxIter 500 end \\%geom MaxIter 500 coordsys redundant cartfallback true ReducePrint true end \\%output Print[ P\\_Basis ] 2 Print[ P\\_MOs ] 1 Print[P\\_hirshfeld] 1 end * xyzfile 0 2 capped\\_square\\_antiprismatic\\_1\\_nunpairedes\\_0\\_charge\\_0\\_xtb.xyz Both files contain ORCA input for geometry optimization and frequency calculations using the PBE0 functional, def2-SVP basis set, D4 dispersion, and other specified settings. perform_dft_calculation Action: Now I'll create the new input files for the distorted geometries while maintaining the exact same configuration as the original files: Tool used: Tool Name: input_file_service Arguments: message2agent: Please create two new ORCA input files: 1. In the cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ folder, create cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp • Use the exact same configuration as in cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp • But replace the geometry line to use cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz instead 2. In the capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ folder, create capped_square_antipris-matic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp • Use the exact same configuration as in capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ.inp • But replace the geometry line to use capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz instead Keep everything else the same as in the original input files, including all computational parameters and settings. input_file_service Action: Tool used: submit_slurm_job Action: Now I'll check the other input file: Tool used: Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please check the content of capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/-capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp to verify the number of cores and any dependencies. interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ_removed.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: The file capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_-FREQ_removed.inp specifies the following regarding cores and dependencies: • Number of cores: 16 (set by %pal nprocs 16) • Memory per core: 4000 MB (set by %maxcore 4000) • SCF autotraH: OFF (set by AutotraH false) • Max SCF and geometry optimization iterations: 500 each • Basis set: def2-SVP with def2-ECP for lanthanoids • Functional: PBE0 • Dispersion: D4 • RIJCOSX approximation and DEFGRID2 grid • TightSCF convergence • Geometry input: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz No external dependencies are referenced beyond the specified basis, ECP, and geometry file. The configuration matches the requirements for a 16-core calculation with the correct settings for a lanthanide complex. submit_slurm_job Action: Based on the verification, both input files: 1. Specify 16 cores (%pal nprocs 16) 2. Use the same level of theory and settings (PBE0/def2-SVP with D4 dispersion) 3. Reference distorted XYZ files as input geometries Now I'll submit both jobs in parallel: Tool used: Tool Name: submit_slurm_jobs Arguments: job_names: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ', 'capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ'] number_of_cores: [16, 16] shell_commands: ['orca cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp &gt; cn9_YICLED_OPT_-FREQ_removed.out', 'orca capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp &gt; capped_-square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.out'] submit_slurm_job Action: I've successfully submitted both ORCA jobs in parallel. Both calculations completed successfully with \"ORCA TERMINATED NORMALLY\" status. Here's a summary: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ (using cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp) • Job ID: 230632 • Status: Completed normally • Cores used: 16 2. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ (using capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_-FREQ_removed.inp) • Job ID: 230633 • Status: Completed normally • Cores used: 16 Both jobs used the specified input files that reference distorted geometries as their starting points. The calculations used PBE0/def2-SVP with D4 dispersion, RIJCOSX approximation, and def2-ECP for lanthanoids, as specified in the input files. Output files (including the main .out file, optimized geometries, and trajectory files) have been generated in their respective directories: -cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out -cn9_YICLED_OPT_-FREQ_removed.xyz -cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed_trj.xyz -capped_square_antipris-matic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.out -capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.xyz -capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed_trj.xyz The jobs ran smoothly without any errors. run_orca Action: I've successfully run both ORCA jobs in parallel. Here's a summary of the results: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ calculation: • Input file: cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp • Job ID: 230632 • Status: Completed successfully (\"ORCA TERMINATED NORMALLY\") • Used 16 cores as specified in the input file • Output files generated: -cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out (main output) -cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.xyz (optimized structure) -cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed_trj.xyz (trajectory file) 2. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ calculation: • Input file: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp • Job ID: 230633 • Status: Completed successfully (\"ORCA TERMINATED NORMALLY\") • Used 16 cores as specified in the input file • Output files generated: -capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.out (main output) -capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.xyz (optimized structure) -capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed_trj.xyz (trajectory file) Both calculations used PBE0/def2-SVP with D4 dispersion, RIJCOSX approximation, and def2-ECP for lanthanoids (Ce) as specified in the input files. Both jobs started from the distorted geometries provided in the respective _distorted.xyz files. perform_dft_calculation Action:Now, let me check if the new calculations completed successfully:Tool used:Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please check the output files for the new calculations to determine if they converged successfully: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out 2. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.out For each calculation, look for \"ORCA TERMINATED NORMALLY\" message and verify that both the geometry optimization and frequency calculations completed successfully. Please report if there are any errors or warnings that need attention.interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used:Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out query_keys: ['convergence_information'] interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: extract_properties_from_orca_outputfile Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ_removed.out query_keys: ['convergence_information'] interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ_removed.out interact_with_os_and_files Action:Both output files were checked for convergence and errors:1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out:• SCF converged successfully.• Geometry optimization completed and converged.• No critical errors or warnings, except a note: \"Only C1 symmetry has been detected, increase convergence thresholds\" (not critical for convergence). 2. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_-FREQ_removed.out:• SCF converged successfully.• Geometry optimization completed and converged.• No critical errors or warnings, except a note: \"Only C1 symmetry has been detected, increase convergence thresholds\" (not critical for convergence). Both calculations converged successfully for both geometry optimization and frequency steps. No significant errors or warnings require attention. 1. I read the original input files to ensure I used the exact same configuration:• cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp • capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ.inp 2. Created new input files with the \"_removed\" suffix while maintaining all computational parameters:• cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp • capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ_removed.inp 3. Updated the geometry lines in the new input files to use the distorted geometries:• Changed to use cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz • Changed to use capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz 4. Ran both ORCA calculations in parallel using the same settings:• PBE0 functional • def2-SVP basis set with def2-ECP for Ce • D4 dispersion correction • RIJCOSX approximation • DEFGRID2 integration grid • 16 cores per calculation 5. Verified that both calculations completed successfully:• Both calculations converged for both geometry optimization and frequency parts • Output files were generated with the \"_removed\" suffix as requested • No critical errors or warnings were found The calculations were completed successfully and all specified output files are now available in their respective folders.remove_imaginary_frequency Action: Now, let's check if the new calculations still have any imaginary frequencies: Tool used: Tool Name: check_imaginary_frequency Arguments: output_file_path_list: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out', 'capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_-1_OPT_FREQ_removed.out'] remove_imaginary_frequency Action:I notice that both structures still have imaginary frequencies after the first optimization round: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out: Imaginary frequency of -85.19 cm -¹ in mode 6 2. capped_-square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ_removed.out: Imaginary frequency of -14.79 cm -¹ in mode 6 For the capped_square_antiprismatic_1 conformer, the imaginary frequency is now -14.79 cm -¹, which is less than 15 cm -¹ in absolute value. According to our criteria, this can be properly ignored, so we don't need to optimize this structure further. However, the cn9_YICLED conformer still has a significant imaginary frequency of -85.19 cm -¹, so we need to perform another round of optimization for this structure. Let's generate the trajectory file for the remaining structure with significant imaginary frequency:Tool used: Tool Name: generate_trajectory_files Arguments: output_file_path_list: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out'] number_of_mode_list: [6] remove_imaginary_frequency Action: Now let's parse the new distorted xyz coordinates for the cn9_YICLED conformer: Tool used: Tool Name: parse_distored_xyz_image Arguments: xyz_trajectory_file_names: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.out.v006.xyz'] distored_xyz_file_names: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_re-moved_distorted.xyz'] remove_imaginary_frequency Action:Now, let's perform a second round of optimization for the cn9_YICLED conformer:Tool used:Tool Name: perform_dft_calculation Arguments: message2agent: Please make sure to read the cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_-FREQ_removed.inp file and use the exact same configuration for the new calculation, simply replace the xyz file in the geometry line. The new calculation is about performing opt and freq calculation with the cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed_distorted.xyz file. Please name the output file cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed2.out. Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: The contents of cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp are: ! OPT FREQ PBE0 def2-SVP D4 RIJCOSX DEFGRID2 TightSCF \\%maxcore 4000 \\%pal nprocs 16 end \\%basis Basis \"def2-SVP\" ECP \"def2-ECP\" end \\%scf AutotraH false MaxIter 500 end \\%geom MaxIter 500 coordsys redundant cartfallback true ReducePrint true end \\%output Print[ P\\_Basis ] 2 Print[ P\\_MOs ] 1 Print[P\\_hirshfeld] 1 end * xyzfile 0 2 cn9\\_YICLED\\_OPT\\_FREQ\\_distorted.xyz perform_dft_calculation Action: Now, I'll create a new input file for the new calculation with the exact same configuration, only changing the geometry file: Tool used: Tool Name: input_file_service Arguments: message2agent: Please create a new ORCA input file in the cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ folder named cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed2.inp. Use exactly the same configuration as in cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed.inp, but replace the geometry line to use cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed_distorted.xyz instead of cn9_YICLED_-OPT_FREQ_distorted.xyz. Keep all other computational parameters exactly the same as in the original input file. input_file_service Action: Tool used: Tool Name: generate_geometry_line Arguments: message2agent: generate the geometry line for cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ_removed_distorted.xyz, the molecule(s) are Ce(III) complex with 3 nitrate_bi and 3 water ligands, the 