charge analysis\n\t\tMulliken, Löwdin\n\t\t\n\t\n\tand an image of the optimized structure. Organic Compounds","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"2 Level 2 Query: Perform in parallel geometry optimization using the xyz files listed below using ORCA with the Hartree-Fock (HF) method and def2-SVP basis set in the gas phase. Once the calculations have been successfully completed, please generate individual reports for each of the molecules listed below","anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"D-Glucose_Pubchem\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\txyz (charge = 0; multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"xyz (charge = 0; multiplicity = 1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"L-Phenylalanine_Zwitterion_Openbabel\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\txyz (charge = 0; multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"_2-cyclohexanediol_openbabel.xyz (charge = 0; multiplicity = 1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"L-Histidine_Non_Zwitterion_Openbabel\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\txyz (charge = 0; multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"_2-biphenol_openbabel.xyz (charge = 0; multiplicity = 1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"R-3-hydroxycyclopentan-1-one_openbabel.xyz (charge = 0; multiplicity = 1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"3-methylbutanoate_anion_openbabel.xyz (charge = -1; multiplicity = 1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"xyz (charge = -1; multiplicity = 1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"computational_chemist Action: Computational Chemistry Task: HF/def2-SVP Optimization and Analysis I&apos;ll perform parallel geometry optimizations for the 20 organic compounds using ORCA with HF/def2-SVP, followed by comprehensive analysis of each molecule. Step 1: Organize files and create folders for each molecule Tool used: Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Create folders for each molecule and move the corresponding XYZ files into them. Here are the molecules: 1. caffeine_openbabel.xyz 2. theobromine_openbabel.xyz 3. aspirin_openbabel.xyz 4\n\t\tcreatinine_amine_tautomer_openbabel.xyz 10. creatinine_imine_- tautomer_openbabel.xyz 11. L-phenylalanine_zwitterion_openbabel.xyz 12. 2-chloronitrobenzene_- openbabel.xyz 13. cis-1_2-cyclohexanediol_openbabel.xyz 14. L-histidine_non_zwitterion_openba- bel.xyz 15. 2_2-biphenol_openbabel.xyz 16. S-2-ethyl-2-fluoropentan-1-ol_openbabel.xyz 17. R-3- hydroxycyclopentan-1-one_openbabel.xyz 18. 3\n\t\n\t\n\t\tmethyl_salicylate_openbabel.xyz 5. acetaminophen_openbabel.xyz 6. triazaadaman-tane_openbabel.xyz 7. limonene_openbabel.xyz\n\t\t\n\t\t\t8\n\t\t\n\t\n\tD-glucose_pubchem.xyz (if this doesn&apos;t exist, try D-glucose_openbabel.xyz) 9 -methylbutanoate_anion_openbabel.xyz 19. diiso-propylamide_anion_openbabel.xyz 20. diisopropylammonium_cation_openbabel.xyz computational_chemist Action: Step 2: Set up ORCA input files and prepare for optimization Tool used: Tool Name: geometry_optimization Arguments: message2agent: Optimize all the following molecules in parallel using ORCA with HF/def2-SVP method in the gas phase. Here are the molecules with their charge and multiplicity: 1. caffeine: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1 2 theobromine: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1 3. aspirin: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1 4. methyl_salicylate: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1 5. acetaminophen: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1 6. triazaadamantane: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1 7. limonene: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"computational_chemist Action: Computational Chemistry Task: HF/def2-SVP Optimization and Analysis I&apos;ll perform parallel geometry optimizations for the 20 organic compounds using ORCA with HF/def2-SVP, followed by comprehensive analysis of each molecule. Step 1: Organize files and create folders for each molecule Tool used: Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Create folders for each molecule and move the corresponding XYZ files into them. Here are the molecules: 1. caffeine_openbabel.xyz 2. theobromine_openbabel.xyz 3. aspirin_openbabel.xyz 4","anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"D-Glucose\n\t\t\n\t\tcharge = 0, multiplicity = 1 9. creatinine_amine_tautomer: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"creatinine_imine_tautomer: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"L-phenylalanine_zwitterion: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1 12. 2-chloronitrobenzene: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1 13. cis-1_2-cyclohexanediol: charge = 0\n\t\tmultiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"L-histidine_non_zwitterion: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1 15. 2_2-biphenol: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"S-2-ethyl-2-fluoropentan-1-ol: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"R-3-hydroxycyclopentan-1-one: charge = 0, multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Complete the following request: Perform in parallel geometry optimization of the [compounds below] using ORCA with the Hartree-Fock (HF) method and def2-SVP basis set in the gas phase. Once the calculations have been successfully completed, please generate individual reports for each of the molecules listed below, one at a time\n\t\n\t\n\t\tEach report should include the final Cartesian coordinates (in Å), total energy (in Hartrees), point group symmetry, dipole moment (in Debye), molecular orbital analysis (including an MO energy table and the HOMO-LUMO gap), atomic charge analysis\n\t\tMulliken, Löwdin\n\t\t\n\t\n\tDo not ask for my confirmation this time and an image of the optimized structure Inorganic Compounds","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"Complete the following request: Perform in parallel geometry optimization of the [compounds below] using ORCA with the Hartree-Fock (HF) method and def2-SVP basis set in the gas phase. Once the calculations have been successfully completed, please generate individual reports for each of the molecules listed below, one at a time","anchors":[]},{"raw_text":") hexacarbonyl (low spin) -SMILES: [Cr](=C=O)(=C=O)(=C=O)(=C=O)(=C=O)(=C=O)\n\t\t\n\t\t\tChromium","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Chlorine trifluoride -SMILES: FCl(F)F","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Fluorophosphoric acid (singly deprotonated form) -SMILES: [O-]P(F)(O)=O InOrganicMoleculesGeometryOptimizationAndProperties_level1_7 computational_chemist Action: List of Inorganic Compounds: 1\n\t\t\n\t\n\tchromium_hexacarbonyl_.xyz (charge = 0; multiplicity = 1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"xyz (charge = -1; multiplicity = 1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"cyclohexyldimethylphosphine.xyz (charge = 0; multiplicity = 1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"xyz (charge = -1; multiplicity = 1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"xyz (charge = -1; multiplicity = 1)\n\t\t\n\t\t\thexafluorophosphate","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"xyz (charge = -1; multiplicity = 1)\n\t\t\n\t\t\tdicyanoaurate","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"xenon_tetrafluoride.xyz (charge = 0\n\t\tmultiplicity = 1) Tool used: Tool Name: geometry_generation Arguments: message2agent: Please generate geometries for the following molecules using their SMILES strings","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"C1CCC1 2. methylcyclopropane: CC1CC1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"C1CCCC1 4. methylcyclobutane: CC1CCC1 5. cyclohexane: C1CCCCC1 6. methylcyclopentane: CC1CCCC1 7. cycloheptane: C1CCCCCC1 8. methylcyclohexane: CC1CCCCC1","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Tool used: Tool Name: geometry_optimization Arguments: message2agent: Please optimize all 10 molecules using B3LYP/6-31G(d) and calculate frequencies for each one. Create a separate folder for each molecule. All molecules have charge 0 and multiplicity 1\n\t\tcyclooctane: C1CCCCCCC1 10. methylcycloheptane: CC1CCCCCC1\n\t\t\n\t\n\tName the files according to their molecule names. computational_chemist Action: Now let&apos;s proceed with optimizing the geometries and calculating frequencies using B3LYP/6-31G(d) Use the following initial geometries: 1. cyclobutane: cyclobutane_initial.xyz 2. methylcyclopropane: methylcyclopropane_initial.xyz 3. cyclopentane: cyclopentane_initial.xyz","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Please ensure that frequency calculations are performed to obtain enthalpy and Gibbs free energy values. Use DFT level optimization with B3LYP/6-31G(d)\n\t\tmethylcycloheptane: methylcycloheptane_initial.xyz\n\t\t\n\t\n\tcomputational_chemist","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Tool used: Tool Name: post_analysis_expert Arguments: message2agent: I need to calculate the ring strain energies for cycloalkanes (n=3 to 8) based on the reaction energies for the conversions cyclo(CnH2n) → cyclo(Cn-1H2n-3)-CH3. Here are the thermochemical data for all molecules: 1. cyclobutane: Enthalpy = -156.97750588 Eh, Gibbs free energy = -157.00875190 Eh 2. methylcyclopropane: Enthalpy = -156.97713034 Eh, Gibbs free energy = -157.00924107 Eh 3. cyclopentane: Enthalpy = -196.26049950 Eh, Gibbs free energy = -196.29503294 Eh 4. methylcyclobutane: Enthalpy = -196.23527570 Eh, Gibbs free energy\n\t\t314.05417626 Eh 10. methylcycloheptane: Enthalpy = -314.02117351\n\t\n\t\n\t\tGibbs free energy = -274.81439009 Eh 9. cyclooctane: Enthalpy = -314.01339019 Eh, Gibbs free energy\n\t\t\n\t\n\tAction: Now that all geometry optimizations and frequency calculations are complete, let&apos;s calculate the reaction energies and ring strain energies Eh, Gibbs free energy = -235.55428898 Eh 7. cycloheptane: Enthalpy = -274.76056827 Eh, Gibbs free energy = -274.79974877 Eh 8. methylcyclohexane: Enthalpy = -274.77587934 Eh Eh, Gibbs free energy = -314.06287101 Eh Please: 1. Calculate the ∆H and ∆G for each reaction: cyclo(CnH2n) → cyclo(Cn-1H2n-3)-CH3 for n=4 to 8. 2. Calculate the ring strain energies using first cyclooctane (n=8) as the reference (zero strain), then recalculate using cyclohexane (n=6) as the reference. 3. Provide the ring strain energies in both kcal/mol and kJ/mol. 4. Format the results as tables for use in a final report. computational_chemist Action: Now let&apos;s create the final report using the calculated ring strain energies Tool used: Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please create a file named &apos;report.md&apos; with the following content: Calculated Gibbs Free Energies (Hartree) Molecule Gibbs Free Energy (Hartree) Acetic acid -228.93401544 Acetate ion -228.46232720","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"Tool used: Tool Name: post_analysis_expert Arguments: message2agent: I need to calculate the ring strain energies for cycloalkanes (n=3 to 8) based on the reaction energies for the conversions cyclo(CnH2n) → cyclo(Cn-1H2n-3)-CH3. Here are the thermochemical data for all molecules: 1. cyclobutane: Enthalpy = -156.97750588 Eh, Gibbs free energy = -157.00875190 Eh 2. methylcyclopropane: Enthalpy = -156.97713034 Eh, Gibbs free energy = -157.00924107 Eh 3. cyclopentane: Enthalpy = -196.26049950 Eh, Gibbs free energy = -196.29503294 Eh 4. methylcyclobutane: Enthalpy = -196.23527570 Eh, Gibbs free energy","anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Fluoroacetic acid\n\t\t-328.12958016","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Chloroacetic acid\n\t\t-688.46763055","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Chlorofluoroacetic acid\n\t\t-787.66794756","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"-1.09744548\n\t\n\t\n\t\tProton (electronic energy)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Action: Summary of Ce Complex Computational Study I have successfully completed the computational study of the Ce(III) complex with 3 nitrate_bi and 3 water ligands. Here&apos;s a summary of what was accomplished: 1. Initial Geometry Generation: Generated 5 different conformers of the Ce complex with coordination number 9","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Geometry Optimization: Optimized all conformers using ORCA with PBE0/def2-SVP, D4 dispersion, RIJCOSX approximation, DEFGRID2 integration grid, and def2-ECP for Ce. For conformers with imaginary frequencies, additional optimization steps were performed to obtain true minima","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Single Point Calculations: Performed single point calculations on the optimized geometries using ωB97M-V/def2-SVPD with def2-ECP for Ce. All calculations used TightSCF convergence criteria, 16 cores, and a maximum of 500 SCF iterations","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Energy Analysis: Extracted and analyzed energies for all conformers, identifying the most stable structure as the capped_square_antiprismatic_0 conformer","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Visualization: Generated a visualization of the most stable conformer","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Final Report: Created a comprehensive report detailing the energy differences between conformers in both the optimization and single point calculation levels","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Key Results: -The most stable conformer is capped_square_antiprismatic_0 with other conformers having relative energies ranging from 0.10 to 2.59 kcal/mol higher. -The energetic ordering from optimization level (PBE0/def2-SVP) differs slightly from the single point calculation level (ωB97M-V/def2-SVPD), highlighting the importance of using a high-level method for final energy evaluations\n\t\t\n\t\n\tAll results have been organized in the Final_Report directory, containing the energy analysis report and a visualization of the most stable conformer. computational_chemist","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Action: Energy Results for Ce Complex Conformers Here are the detailed energy values for all five conformers of the Ce(III) complex: Absolute Energies\n\t\t\n\t\n\tin Hartree, Eh","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Conformer PBE0/def2-SVP (Optimization) ωB97M-V/def2-SVPD\n\t\tSingle Point","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]}],"layout_json":null,"tei_xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<TEI xml:space=\"preserve\" xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" \nxmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" \nxsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kermitt2/grobid/master/grobid-home/schemas/xsd/Grobid.xsd\"\n xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\t<teiHeader xml:lang=\"en\">\n\t\t<fileDesc>\n\t\t\t<titleStmt>\n\t\t\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">El Agente: An Autonomous Agent for Quantum Chemistry</title>\n\t\t\t\t<funder>\n\t\t\t\t\t<orgName type=\"full\">Vector Institute</orgName>\n\t\t\t\t</funder>\n\t\t\t\t<funder ref=\"#_ebGvTAK\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<orgName type=\"full\">ONR</orgName>\n\t\t\t\t</funder>\n\t\t\t\t<funder ref=\"#_mgHcGkU #_S3HeQU6\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<orgName type=\"full\">NSERC</orgName>\n\t\t\t\t</funder>\n\t\t\t\t<funder ref=\"#_C7hvKMm\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<orgName type=\"full\">King Abdullah University of Science and Technology</or