sponse. The File I/O Agent has a forgetting mechanism where its context is deleted every time it finishes a subtask, so its final context length is reported for each usage.</p></div>\n<div xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\"><head>Agent Final Context Length</head></div>\n<div xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\"><head>Computational Chemistry Agent 19855</head><p>Geometry Visualization Agent 6527 File I/O Agent 7572 File I/O Agent 18274 Geometry Optimization Agent 17509 DFT Agent 30588 File I/O Agent 8070 ORCA Execution Agent 17801 SLURM Agent 17345 Input File Expert Agent 21174 Geometry Line Expert Agent 1737 Parallelization Expert Agent 1155 Memory Allocation Expert Agent 498 Configuration Recommendation Agent 612 Runtype Expert Agent 852 File I/O Agent 7463 Imaginary Frequency Removal Agent 6910 File I/O Agent 4396 File I/O Agent 3249 File I/O Agent 3026 Geometry Generation Agent 10176 Table S8 Evaluation rubric summarizing assessment criteria and weight percentages for each question type and difficulty level across Level 1 &amp; Level 2 computational chemistry tasks. Question Type Difficulty Criterion Weight (%) Organic Compounds Level 1 Correct input file -level of theory, required keywords, charge, and multiplicity Convergence of calculation -SCF, geometry optimization, and absence of imaginary frequency Report generation Successful extraction and documentation of all report values, including image generation Successful generation of XYZ from SMILES Organic Compounds Level 2 Correct input file -level of theory, required keywords, charge, and multiplicity Convergence of calculation -SCF, geometry optimization, and absence of imaginary frequency Report generation Successful extraction and documentation of all report values, including image generation Inorganic Compounds Level 1 Correct input file -level of theory, required keywords, charge, and multiplicity Convergence of calculation -SCF, geometry optimization, and absence of imaginary frequency Report genera