sonable value for pKa (around -3 to 3) Absorption spectrum of organic molecules Level 1 &amp; Level 2 Correct input file (level of theory as requested, 'tddft' block) Calculation completed normally Extract and report the values correctly, and the number matched B.2 Organic Compounds B.2.1 Level 1 Query: Perform in parallel geometry optimization of the [compounds below] using ORCA with the Hartree-Fock (HF) method and def2-SVP basis set in the gas phase. Once the calculations have been successfully completed, please generate individual reports for each of the molecules listed below, one at a time. Each report should include the final Cartesian coordinates (in Å), total energy (in Hartrees), point group symmetry, dipole moment (in Debye), molecular orbital analysis (including an MO energy table and the HOMO-LUMO gap), atomic charge analysis (Mulliken, Löwdin, and Hirshfeld), and an image of the optimized structure. Organic Compounds: 1. caffeine (SMILES: CN1C=NC2=C1C(=O)N(C(=O)N2C)C) 2. theobromine (SMILES: CN1C=NC2=C1C(=O)NC(=O)N2C) 3. acetylsalicylic_acid (SMILES: CC(=O)OC1=CC=CC=C1C(=O)O) folder: OrganicMoleculesGeometryOptimizationAndProperties_level1_1 computational_chemist Action: Computational Chemistry Task: Geometry Optimization and Property Analysis</p><p>I'll perform the parallel geometry optimization of caffeine, theobromine, and acetylsalicylic acid using ORCA with HF/def2-SVP, followed by detailed property analysis.</p></div>\n<div xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\"><head>Step 1: Generate initial geometries for all three molecules</head><p>Tool used:</p><p>Tool Name: geometry_generation Arguments: message2agent: Generate geometries for the following three molecules using their SMILES representations:</p><p>1. caffeine: CN1C=NC2=C1C(=O)N(C(=O)N2C)C 2. theobromine: CN1C=NC2=C1C(=O)NC(=O)N2C 3. acetylsalicylic acid: CC(=O)OC1=CC=CC=C1C(=O)O Please prepare all three initial geometries.</p><p>computational_chemist Action: Let me first organize the files into appropriate folders and then perform the geometry optimizations using ORCA with HF/def2-SVP.</p></div>\n<div xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\"><head>Tool used:</head><p>Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please organize the initial geometry files into separate folders for each molecule: 1. Create a folder named \"caffeine\" and move caffeine_initial.xyz there 2. Create a folder named \"theobromine\" and move theobromine_initial.xyz there 3. Create a folder named \"acetylsalicylic_acid\" and move acetylsalicylic_acid_initial.xyz there</p><p>computational_chemist Action: Tool Name: geometry_optimization Arguments: message2agent: Perform geometry optimization for all three molecules (caffeine, theobromine, and acetylsalicylic acid) in parallel using ORCA with the following specifications: -Method: Hartree-Fock (HF) -Basis set: def2-SVP -Environment: gas phase -Charge for caffeine: 0, multiplicity: 1 -Charge for theobromine: 0, multiplicity: 1 -Charge for acetylsalicylic acid: 0, multiplicity: 1 For each molecule, please use the initial geometry file in its respective folder.</p><p>computational_chemist Action: 3.1 Process Caffeine Tool used: Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Extract the following properties from the caffeine_HF_OPT_FREQ/caffeine_-HF_OPT_FREQ.out file and provide them in a structured format: 1. Final Cartesian coordinates (in Å) 2. Total energy (in Hartrees) 3. Point group symmetry 4. Dipole moment (in Debye) 5. Molecular orbital analysis (MO energy table and HOMO-LUMO gap) 6. Atomic charge analysis (Mulliken, Löwdin, and Hirshfeld) Please format the output as separate markdown sections. computational_chemist Action: Now let's generate a visualization of the optimized caffeine structure: Tool used: Tool Name: geometry_visualization Arguments: message2agent: Please visualize the optimized geometry of caffeine from caffeine_HF_OPT_-FREQ/caffeine_HF_OPT_FREQ.xyz file. computational_chemist A