hod and def2-SVP basis set in the gas phase. Individual comprehensive reports have been generated for each molecule.</p></div>\n<div xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\"><head>Summary of Steps Completed:</head><p>1. Initial Geometry Generation:</p><p>• Created initial geometries for all three molecules from their SMILES representations • All molecules were identified with charge 0 and multiplicity 1 2. File Organization:</p><p>• Organized files into separate directories for each molecule 3. Geometry Optimization:</p><p>• Performed preliminary optimization using xtb • Conducted full HF/def2-SVP optimizations with frequency calculations • Verified all structures reached stable minima (no imaginary frequencies) 4. Data Extraction and Visualization: • Extracted comprehensive data from output files including: -Final Cartesian coordinates -Total energy values -Dipole moments -Molecular orbital energies and HOMO-LUMO gaps -Atomic charge analyses (Mulliken, Löwdin, and Hirshfeld) • Created visualizations of the optimized structures 5. Report Generation: • Generated detailed reports for each molecule in Markdown format • Saved reports in a dedicated 'reports' directory Results Summary: Molecule Total Energy (Hartrees) HOMO-LUMO Gap (eV) Dipole Moment (Debye) Caffeine -675.83732469 11.81 4.33 Theobromine -636.83781921 11.83 4.94 Acetylsalicylic Acid -644.47944566 11.70 2.30</p><p>The reports containing all requested information (coordinates, energies, symmetry, dipole moments, MO analysis, charge analysis, and structure images) can be found in the 'reports' directory: -reports/-caffeine_report.md -reports/theobromine_report.md -reports/acetylsalicylic_acid_report.md All calculations were performed successfully and the requested analysis has been completed.</p><p>18. 3-methylbutanoate_anion: charge = -1, multiplicity = 1 19. diisopropylamide_anion: charge = -1, multiplicity = 1 20. diisopropylammonium_cation: charge = +1, multiplicity = 1 For all calculations, use ORCA with t