es to determine any dependencies and resource requirements:</p><p>Tool used: Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please check the number of cores required for the ORCA calculations in the following input files and identify any dependent files: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_-YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp 2. tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_-FREQ.inp 3. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_-FREQ.inp 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_-OPT_FREQ.inp 5. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_-1_OPT_FREQ.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_-FREQ.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_-OPT_FREQ.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_-OPT_FREQ.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: Here is the summary for the number of cores and dependent files for each ORCA input file: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp • Number of cores: 16 (specified by nprocs 16 in the %pal block) • Dependent file: cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_0_nunpairedes_0_charge_-0_xtb.xyz 2. tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.inp • Number of cores: 16 • Dependent file: tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_0_nun-pairedes_0_charge_0_xtb.xyz 3. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ.inp • Number of cores: 16 • Dependent file: tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_pris-matic_1_nunpairedes_0_charge_0_xtb.xyz 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_-FREQ.inp • Number of cores: 16 • Dependent file: capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antipris-matic_0_nunpairedes_0_charge_0_xtb.xyz 5. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_-FREQ.inp • Number of cores: 16 • Dependent file: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antipris--Geometry optimization and frequency calculation: ! OPT FREQ PBE0 def2-SVP D4 RIJCOSX DEFGRID2 TightSCF -Basis set: def2-SVP with def2-ECP for lanthanoids -SCF settings: AutotraH false, MaxIter 500, TightSCF true -Geometry settings: MaxIter 500, coordsys redundant, cartfallback true, ReducePrint true -Output settings: Various print levels for basis, MOs, and Hirshfeld analysis -Input coordinates: * xyzfile 0 2 cn9_YICLED_0_nunpairedes_0_charge_0_xtb.xyz Summary: The calculation is set to use 16 cores, 4000 MB per core, and includes all required dependencies for a PBE0/def2-SVP geometry optimization and frequency calculation with D4 dispersion and RIJCOSX. The input file is fully configured for the specified Ce(III) complex. submit_slurm_job Action: I've verified the first input file which confirms the use of 16 cores (%pal nprocs 16 end). Let me check the remaining files to ensure consistency: Tool used: Tool Name: interact_with_os_and_files Arguments: message2agent: Please check the content of the remaining input files to verify the core count and dependencies: 1. tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_-FREQ.inp 2. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_-FREQ.inp 3. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_-OPT_FREQ.inp 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_-1_OPT_FREQ.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.inp Tool Name