_nunpairedes\\_0\\_charge\\_0\\_xtb.xyz 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_-FREQ.inp: ! OPT FREQ PBE0 def2-SVP D4 RIJCOSX DEFGRID2 TightSCF \\%maxcore 4000 \\%pal nprocs 16 end \\%basis Basis \"def2-SVP\" ECP \"def2-ECP\" end \\%scf AutotraH false MaxIter 500 ConvCriteria Tight end \\%geom MaxIter 500 coordsys redundant cartfallback true ReducePrint true end \\%output Print[ P\\_Basis ] 2 Print[ P\\_MOs ] 1 Print[P\\_hirshfeld] 1 end * xyzfile 0 2 capped\\_square\\_antiprismatic\\_1\\_nunpairedes\\_0\\_charge\\_0\\_xtb.xyz All files have been read and their content is shown above for your verification. submit_slurm_job Action: Good news! All input files have been corrected with the proper SCF settings. The previous issue has been addressed by changing: -From: TightSCF (in SCF block) -To: ConvCriteria Tight (in SCF block) All files now have 16 cores specified in the \\%pal block and have their required dependencies (xyz files) present in their respective directories. I'll now submit all five jobs in parallel: Tool used: Tool Name: submit_slurm_jobs Arguments: job_names: ['cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ', 'tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ', 'tricapped_trig-onal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ', 'capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ', 'capped_square_-antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ'] number_of_cores: [16, 16, 16, 16, 16] shell_commands: ['orca cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp &gt; cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.out', 'orca tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.inp &gt; tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.out', 'orca tri-capped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ.inp &gt; tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ.out', 'orca capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ.inp &gt; capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_-FREQ.out', 'orca capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ.inp &gt; capped_square_antipris-matic_1_OPT_FREQ.out'] submit_slurm_job Action:</p><p>I have submitted all five ORCA jobs in parallel using 16 cores for each job as specified. Each job received a unique SLURM job ID:</p><p>1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ -Job ID: 230613 2. tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ -Job ID: 230614 3. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ -Job ID: 230615 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ -Job ID: 230616 5. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ -Job ID: 230617 Unfortunately, the calculations encountered another error. This time the error is related to the \"ConvCriteria\" parameter: [file orca\\_tools/Tool-Scanner/qcscan1.cpp, line 106]: Unknown identifier in SCF block line 13: Last token: CONVCRITERIA. The error indicates that the \"ConvCriteria\" parameter in the SCF block is not recognized by this version of ORCA. This is a syntax issue with the SCF convergence criteria settings in the input files. The version of ORCA installed on this system does not appear to support either \"TightSCF\" (the previous error) or \"ConvCriteria\" (the current error) in the SCF block as they are currently formatted.</p><p>To successfully run these calculations, the input files would need to be further modified to use SCF convergence parameters that are compatible with the installed ORCA version.</p><p>run_orca Action:</p><p>Let me try to fix the input files by completely removing the problematic part of the SCF block:</p><p>Tool used: Tool Name: input_file_service Arguments: message2agent: The ERROR MESSAGE IS \"Unknown identifier in SCF block line 13: Last token: CONVCRITERIA.\" Please debug all five input files and completely remove the ConvCriteria line from the SCF block. Instead, let ORCA use its default convergence settings. Fix these files: 1. cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ/cn9_YICLED_OPT_FREQ.inp 2. tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_-FREQ/tri_tri_mer_capped_OPT_FREQ.inp 3. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ/tri-capped_trigonal_prismatic_OPT_FREQ.inp 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ/-capped_square_antiprismatic_0_OPT_FREQ.inp 5. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FRE-Q/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_OPT_FREQ.inp input_file_service Action: Tool used: Tool Name: repl_tool Arguments: code: omitted for brevity... input_file