ndencies: 1. tri_tri_mer_capped_SP/tri_tri_mer_capped_SP.inp 2. tricapped_trigonal_pris-matic_SP/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_SP.inp 3. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_SP/capped_-square_antiprismatic_0_SP.inp 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_SP/capped_square_antipris-matic_1_SP.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: Tool used: Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: tri_tri_mer_capped_SP/tri_tri_mer_capped_SP.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_SP/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_SP.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_0_SP/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_SP.inp Tool Name: read_file_content Arguments: file_path: capped_square_antiprismatic_1_SP/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_SP.inp interact_with_os_and_files Action: The contents of the four input files have been checked for core count and dependencies: 1. tri_tri_mer_capped_SP/tri_tri_mer_capped_SP.inp 2. tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_SP/tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_SP.inp 3. capped_square_antiprismatic_0_SP/capped_square_antiprismatic_0_SP.inp 4. capped_square_antiprismatic_1_SP/capped_square_antiprismatic_1_SP.inp Summary of findings: -All input files specify the use of 16 cores via the block: \\%pal nprocs 16 end -All input files use the following dependencies: -Functional: wB97M-V -Basis set: def2-SVPD -Dispersion: VV10 -Effective Core Potential (ECP): def2-ECP -SCF settings: TightSCF, AutotraH false, MaxIter 500 -Output settings: Print[ P_Basis ] 2, Print[ P_MOs ] 1, Print[P_hirshfeld] 1 No discrepancies were found in the core count or dependencies across the files. All are consistent with the specified requirements. Tool Name: submit_slurm_jobs Arguments: job_names: ['cn9_YICLED_SP', 'tri_tri_mer_capped_SP', 'tricapped_trigonal_prismatic_SP', 'capped_square_antiprismatic_0_SP', 'capped_square_antiprismatic_1_SP'] number_of_cores: <ref type=\"bibr\">[16,</ref><ref type=\"bibr\">16,</ref><ref type=\"bibr\">16,</ref><re